        "**Droping unwanted columns and excluding California total:**\n",
        "\n",
        " To avoid data leakage and ensure model generalization, I dropped the Lower_95__CI and Upper_95__CI columns since they are derived from the target variable (Cases).\n",
        "\n",
        " Additionally, I removed rows where the County is listed as \"California\", as these represent aggregate state-level data that would skew the model due to duplicated totals across individual counties."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oliiSnyfx-Ly"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Drop columns that may leak target information\n",
        "df_model = df.drop(columns=[\"Lower_95__CI\", \"Upper_95__CI\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Remove rows where County == \"California\" (state-level total)\n",
        "df_model = df_model[df_model[\"County\"] != \"California\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Preview the cleaned DataFrame\n",
        "df_model.head()\n"
