    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        " **Defining features and target variable, and applying one-hot encoding to categorical variables:**\n",
        "\n",
        "The target variable for this regression task is Cases. The remaining columns will be used as input features. Among them, Disease, County, and Sex are categorical, so I will use one-hot encoding to convert these into a numerical format that can be used by machine learning models."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "j4T2_SzQyg_Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
        "\n",
        "# Separate features and target\n",
        "X = df_model.drop(columns=[\"Cases\"])\n",
        "y = df_model[\"Cases\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define categorical columns\n",
        "categorical_features = [\"Disease\", \"County\", \"Sex\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply one-hot encoding to categorical columns\n",
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "    transformers=[\n",
        "        (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"), categorical_features)\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    remainder=\"passthrough\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Transform the feature matrix\n",
        "X_encoded = preprocessor.fit_transform(X)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AcuDtWAEyGpm"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split the data into training and testing sets:\n",
        "\n",
        "Iam using an 80-20 split, where 80 percent of the data is used for training and 20 percent for testing."
